Quota Sampling
Under this method, the items of the population are subdivided into various groups and then a
quota (number of items to be selected from each subgroup) is fixed. But, within the given guota,
the selection of sample units depends upon the personal judgement of the investigator.
Merits
Reliable Results: If the investigators are skilled and experienced, it gives
more reliable and dependable results.
Economical: The cost of preparing sample and field work is very low.
Demerits
Personal Prejudice: There is considerable risk that a biased sample may be selected
according to the personal prejudice of the investigator.
Not Possible to estimate Sample Error: It is not possible to estimate the sampling error
and the degree of accuracy achieved.
प्रारंBATCH
Convenience Sampling
Under this method, while selecting the sample units the
investigator gives special attention to his convenience.
Merits
Economical: It is less expensive and less time consuming.
Easy Command: The units of the sample are easily located and contacted by the investigators.
Suitable for Pilot Surveys: It is often used for making pilot studies in which questions are pre-tested and
preliminary information is obtained before finalizing the sample design.
Demerits
Next
Toppers
Lack of representation: The units of the sample selected under this method hardly represent the universe.
Personal Prejudice: Convenience samples are prone to bias by their nature.
Unsatisfactory Results: The results obtained under this method are found to be unsatisfactory and misleading.
